# Growth Health Check — beehiiv + SEO + funnel (expanded spec)

**Owner:** Growth. **Supersedes the scope of** the `beehiiv-seo-weekly-check` scheduled task (was: "beehiiv subscribers/posts + GSC vs the SEO plan", Monday weekly). **Requested by Al 2026-07-08:** run **twice a week**, and widen to cover surveys/feedback, lead magnets, everything inside beehiiv, SEO, and Google Trends. Cadence + task edit are Control's to wire (Growth CR `GR-2026-07-08-02`).

## Cadence
**Twice weekly — Monday + Thursday, 07:05.** Silent worker; writes a dated report + surfaces only the top flags to Daily Ops.

## Sources (all live connectors + one Chrome step)
- **beehiiv MCP:** `get_publication_stats`, `get_website_analytics` (+ `_breakdown` pages/referrers), `list_surveys` + `list_survey_responses`, `list_subscribe_forms`, `list_automations` + `get_automation_stats`, `list_posts`/`get_post_stats`.
- **SEO rankings:** Google Search Console (keyword positions/impressions/CTR) via the existing GSC access, checked against the SEO plan target keywords.
- **Google Trends:** `trends.google.com` is JavaScript-rendered, so pull via a **Claude-in-Chrome step** for a fixed observability keyword set; a WebSearch news-scan is the fallback/supplement.
- **Reddit (ingestion, GR-2026-08-10-05, standing rule 2026-08-20):** there is no Reddit MCP and the API is priced out (unauth `.json` 403s), so pull Reddit **via Claude-in-Chrome (signed in), on demand** — with the browser-open caveat — and keep the Gmail `Feeds/Reddit` bridge as the passive net. Do NOT buy the API. Folded into the `mo-content-production` skill (spec 28); this is the standing answer to "we cannot reach Reddit".

## The seven sections (each run)
1. **Subscribers & growth** — active total, new / churned / net; **click-through rate + click-to-open rate as the HEADLINE newsletter engagement metric** (opens are secondary and inflated by Apple Mail Privacy Protection, 2026 refresh); earnings; top acquisition sources.
2. **Website & SEO traffic** — unique visitors / sessions / bounce / session-duration trend; top pages; top referrers; GSC keyword movement vs plan targets.
3. **Lead magnets & funnel** — traffic to `/free-chapter`, `/advisory`, `/products/...chapter-4`, `/book` vs their capture + nurture; **flag any lead-magnet automation still in DRAFT** (a live page with no live follow-up is a leak).
4. **Automations health** — live vs draft; enrolled / completed; open + click; flag unpublished or broken flows and stale test automations.
5. **Surveys & feedback** — new responses since last run; audience makeup (occupation), topic interest, self-reported acquisition channel; and the **contributor/collaboration pool** (subscribers who said Yes/Maybe to contributing and have had no follow-up).
   - **Warm-contributor tracker check (GR-2026-07-08-04).** Read `15_WARM_CONTRIBUTOR_TRACKER.md` every run and raise a flag for any row whose Status is **REPLIED / HOT** but whose "Owed / next action" is still open (a promised piece not sent, a reply not answered). Ahmed Elbendary is the standing example: owed a bylined piece, flag until it ships. A hot contributor going cold from silence is a funnel leak worth a Needs-Allan line.
   - **Nurture-exclusion guard.** Every name in the tracker is personally-outreached and must be **excluded** from the generic Warm Contributors nurture (`seg_dcd86d30`, GR-2026-07-08-03 draft doc 20). Each run, confirm the tracker names are in the automation's exclude set (or carry the "personally-outreached" custom field); flag any tracked contact that is NOT excluded, so a 1:1 promise never gets a mass blast on top.
6. **Rising themes / Google Trends** — rising observability terms feeding the SEO plan + Tech Tuesday / byte-size ideation.
7. **Actions & flags** — 3 to 5 prioritised actions; anything needing Al goes to `Ops_Log.md` "Needs Allan" + the Daily Ops chat.

## Folded-in checklists + mechanisms
- **Beehiiv Ecosystem Health Check (GR-2026-07-30-01, folded in 2026-08-20).** `26_BEEHIIV_ECOSYSTEM_HEALTH_CHECK_2026-07-30.md` is the Beehiiv-specific checklist (profiling coverage, stream fill, automation enrolment, deliverability/auth, list hygiene, inflow integrity) — each item GREEN/AMBER/RED with a threshold + a Beehiiv-MCP method, written to be run by a live agent. It runs inside sections 3-5 here; any RED escalates to Al. **Standing Needs-Allan flags at filing:** profiling coverage ~11% (RED) and stream fill 1/1 (RED — now being addressed by the stream-fill loop below).
- **Native stream-fill loop (GR-2026-08-10-02, folded in 2026-08-20).** The two Role-field streams were near-empty because the Role field was; capture now happens at source. A Monday poll (`post_d35e1d0c` / `poll_9f31d69f`, Technical / Leadership / Both) + three per-choice automations (`aut_782f7d9b` / `aut_48c6e2da` / `aut_c284da01`) write `sub_stream` + send confirmation emails; the stream segments are repointed additively (`seg_eca55c0b` Technical / `seg_566d2362` Leadership = poll preference OR occupation fallback), with a "not set" segment `seg_b67292f1` (~557) + a Thursday reminder `post_f3c48bd2`. The stream-fill check (Beehiiv §2) now monitors this loop growing. **Residual for Al:** re-publish the three confirmation-email edits; confirm per-choice routing on the first live responses.

## Output
Dated report to `07_Website/08_SEO_Improvement_Plan/_Health_Checks/YYYY-MM-DD_health_check.md`; top 3 flags surfaced to Daily Ops.

**Last updated:** 2026-07-08 (Growth), scoped + sample-run once for Al before Control wires it.
